-- target: branch
--
-- LEVEL THE REHEARSAL BRANCH'S SUPERSESSION REGISTER WITH MAIN'S 399 ROWS.
--
-- WHY
-- ---
-- `platform.deprecated_relations` is the platform's register of "this relation moved, and here is
-- what it moved to". The MAIN database carries 399 rows. The rehearsal branch, after the first
-- live BRANCH-REFRESH (2026-09-22 14:58Z), carries **zero** — the refresh's seed set is derived
-- from the catalog ("a `platform` table that ANOTHER table's foreign key points at"), and nothing
-- holds a foreign key to this one, so it was invisible to the derivation and to the five
-- hand-named registries beside it.
--
-- That empty register is not cosmetic. `matrx_records.server.enumeration` decides which registered
-- models are RECORD-BEARING by intersecting matrx-orm's registry with this register, so an empty
-- register is an empty enumeration: on the branch, lane RECORDS-SUITE-2 measured
-- `test_the_enumeration_is_not_empty` and
-- `test_kind_records_go_through_the_door.py::test_the_door_speaks_for_a_relation_the_platform_really_superseded`
-- both red for a reason that has nothing to do with the record store.
--
-- THE CLASS FIX IS IN THE REFRESH, NOT HERE: `scripts/night/branch-refresh.sh` now names
-- `platform.deprecated_relations` in `NAMED_REGISTRIES`, so tomorrow's refresh brings it across on
-- its own and this file becomes a no-op. This file is the instance fix, so the store's package
-- suite can be classified today.
--
-- NO CUSTOMER DATA CROSSES. Every column is a relation NAME and a sentence about a schema change:
-- `old_ref`, `new_ref`, `archived_as`, `reason`, `deprecated_at`. The table has no
-- `organization_id` and no row here names a person, an organization or a value.
--
-- ADDITIVE: one INSERT into an existing register, `on conflict (old_ref) do nothing`, so a branch
-- that has caught up is untouched and a re-run changes nothing. No DDL, no DROP, no REVOKE. The
-- rows below were read from main with a SELECT on 2026-09-22 and are reproduced verbatim.
--
-- lane: RECORDS-SUITE-2

on conflict (old_ref) do nothing;

do $$
declare n int;
begin
    select count(*) into n from platform.deprecated_relations;
    if n < 399 then
        raise exception 'the supersession register carries % rows; main carries 399, and matrx_records.server.enumeration intersects matrx-orm''s registry with this table', n;
    end if;
end $$;
